+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant). Each dish sold
+  uses one portion of its recipe per `qty`, consumed with the ledger `ref`
+  `sale:<ticket>` at `soldAt`. Tickets imported before are skipped. One bad
+  row (`bad_request`) or an item running out (`sale_not_enough_stock`) and
+  nothing is imported; the message names the row (`row 2` is the first data
+  row). Answers `{ "tickets": <count>, "dishes": <count> }`, where `dishes`
+  is the sum of `qty` imported.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists, per item,
+  `theoretical` (recipe use of sales sold in those days, inclusive), `actual`
+  (every `consume` movement in those days) and `difference`
+  (actual − theoretical), for items where either is above zero.
